// ---------- findings (shared statements) ----------
const F1 = 'F1 (MAJOR, blocking): a graduated athlete regains quality in the first EASY week after a restart, with zero established easy weeks. Reproduction p12-return-interplay.mjs: NOVICE, 80 min on 3 days, runMinutes 45, 16 weeks; graduation at the review of week 3; reviews through week 5; nonclinical TRAVEL break 2026-12-14 to 2027-01-12 (30 days, LONG), every elapsed week reviewed as missed; RETURN_AFTER_PAUSE reviewed in week 10 -> REESTABLISH (restart). First EASY week 13 (easyWeeksDone 0, qualityNeeds 0) holds THRESHOLD 3x5 (34 min) with EASY 35 and LONG 39. The EASY_CURRENT comparator under the same timeline has no quality until week 15, two established easy weeks after the switch. Cause: src/r6-program.mjs line 305 sets qualityNeeds=0 at graduation; the restart switch (line 255) resets easyWeeksDone to 0, so runRow (line 230) activates quality at once. Breaches B0-C01 c1 (all R6 quality gates) and R6-RUN-QUALITY C5; DECL-04 consequence. Moderate (18-day) returns are equal for both paths.';
const F2 = 'F2 (MODERATE, blocking): the familiar repeated bouts are prescribed at the full familiar dose after the task has not been performed for more than 28 days, although B0-C02 c1 covers only a current task (R6 intake definition, observed within 28 days) and c5 lapses the status until the task is current again. Reproductions: p13-familiar-bouts.mjs B (10K, 16 weeks): bouts in BUILD weeks 2-6, then NEXT_BLOCK week 13 again at 4x3 (40 min), 49 days after the previous bouts session, while R6 NEXT_BLOCK takes the long run to 0.625 and the easy runs to 0.7 of the peak; p14-bouts-currency.mjs C (half marathon): 56 days; p14 A: a task observed 2026-10-15 or 2026-10-05 (intake 2026-11-01) is first prescribed on 2026-11-17, 33 and 43 days after its last performance (DECL-05 defers the first session two weeks). Currency is read only at intake (src/r6-intake.mjs line 35) and never at the prescription date (src/r6-program.mjs familiarBoutsTask line 319, qualityFor line 342).';
const F3 = 'F3 (MINOR): strides. (a) In the introduction week the strides step 4 -> 5 repetitions (p11-graduation-edges.mjs A, week 4), contrary to B0-C01 c5 (no other run dimension steps); runRow derives the count from executed weeks (src/r6-program.mjs line 229) and the introduction hold covers easy and long only (line 305). (b) Race-day warm-up strides ("easy warm-up with a few relaxed strides", src/r6-prescription.mjs line 61, from src/r6-program.mjs line 998) are not marked optional for EASY_LOW or NOVICE athletes (p41-strides-optional.mjs: easylow-int-10K, novice-10K), contrary to B0-C01 c8; easy, taper and shakeout strides are optional (299 stride sites checked).';
const F4 = 'F4 (MINOR): the CMP.P04 content stage ignores the week wrap. p20-hybrid-content.mjs B2 (10K, STRENGTH goal, familiar bulgarian-split-squat-db, long run day 0 AM, strength days 1, 3, 6 PM): in RUN-led SPECIFIC weeks 7-9 the FULL_B session on day 6 PM keeps bulgarian-split-squat-db x2 13 h before next week\'s long run, while with the strength day before a same-week long run (A2) the row is reduced to 1 set. The CMP.I11 ranking cost sees the wrap (interferenceCosts wrap=true, p20 C) but buildWeek\'s nearProtected (src/r6-program.mjs line 983) reads only same-week runs. B0-C11 c3/c4.';
const F5 = 'F5 (MINOR): the fallback from the familiar bouts is not disclosed as a different stimulus (B0-C02 c3). p13-familiar-bouts.mjs C: two adverse bouts (weeks 2, 3) -> QUALITY REGRESS -> week 4 THRESHOLD 3x5 at step 0 (calibration, correct) with no disclosure, explanation or negotiation item; p14-bouts-currency.mjs B: a 4-day nonclinical break lapses the bouts (src/r6-adaptation.mjs line 1078) with no disclosure either.';
const F6 = 'F6 (MINOR; Product/Data, G03): the observation contract cannot record that the introduction\'s easy alternative (B0-C01 c6) was chosen. Completeness is minutes >= 90% of the plan (src/r6-adaptation.mjs line 124), so an easy run of 31 min reported on the introduced 34-min threshold day is credited as the step-0 calibration: QUALITY ADVANCE, qualityDone 0 -> 1, achieved.quality set (p11-graduation-edges.mjs C); with another step absent it would also step the ladder and count toward the event-specific prerequisite. The default 20-min alternative, honestly reported, is PARTIAL and holds (p10-graduation.mjs C): no penalty, no credit.';
const F7 = 'F7 (MINOR): the calf alternation is decided on template slots before the time fit, so the fitted week can keep only the bent-knee row. p42-calf-alternation.mjs: 570 of 10,526 weeks with calf exposures have a single calf exposure that is bent-knee (seated-calf-raise-db), all with 4 strength days, at 25 (184), 30 (325), 35 (45) and 45 (16) minutes per session; contrary to B0-C05 c2 (straight-knee default whenever the week has a single calf exposure). Selection: src/r7b-repertoire.mjs lines 249-252; fit: src/r6-program.mjs line 977.';

